// Back-fill the parsed tables from rows that reached the raw tables BEFORE the update policies existed
// (update policies only process data ingested after they're created):
//   RdmTrustRaw  -> Trust* tables (Lab 04);  RdmDarwinRaw -> DarwinLocations via ParseDarwinLocations() (Lab 04b).
// Legacy Darwin rows in RdmTrustRaw (from before Lab 04b, when Darwin shared that table) are NOT back-filled
// and shouldn't be moved. Clear them instead: `.clear table RdmTrustRaw data` and `.clear table DarwinLocations data`,
// then point Lab 04 at the NWR Train Movements topic and add Darwin in Lab 04b (see the Lab 04b troubleshooting table).
// Run ONCE: select the whole file (Ctrl+A) and Run, or: python fabric/scripts/apply_kql.py --file fabric/kql/08_backfill.kql
// Each command appends, so running it twice creates duplicates. Commands that find no matching rows just append nothing.
.execute database script with (ContinueOnErrors=true) <|
.set-or-append DarwinLocations <| ParseDarwinLocations()

.set-or-append TrustMovements <| ParseMovements(ExpandTrustRdm())

.set-or-append TrustActivations <| ParseActivations(ExpandTrustRdm())

.set-or-append TrustCancellations <| ParseCancellations(ExpandTrustRdm())

.set-or-append TrustOtherEvents <| ParseOtherTrust(ExpandTrustRdm())
